¶ This scheme gives first the Hypodoric [Eolic, or Locrian] scale⁎ for two Octaves, and then an added tetrachord which introduces a *b*♭ in addition to the *b*, and thus, in modern language, allows of modulation from the principal scale into that of the subdominant.†

